# Chartink Parity Upgrade: Multi-Bar Offsets, Advanced Indicators, Nested Groups & Webhook/Telegram Alerts

This implementation plan brings **TejStockAI** to full parity with and beyond Chartink by implementing the 4 core capabilities that were previously unique to Chartink/Atlas:

1. **Multi-Bar Offset Indexing (`[-1]`, `[-2]`, `[-N]` past candle comparison)**
2. **Advanced Technical Indicators Catalog (VWAP, ATR, ADX, Pivot Points, Stochastics, Ichimoku Cloud)**
3. **Custom Nested Sub-Groups (`(Condition 1 AND 2) OR (Condition 3 AND 4)`)**
4. **Direct External Alerts Engine (Telegram Bot & Webhook Dispatcher for Algo Trading / Tradetron / Broker APIs)**

---

## Proposed Architecture & Changes

### 1. Indicators & Multi-Bar Data Engine
#### [MODIFY] [market-service.js](file:///c:/Users/TEJAS%20KUMAR%20DEWANGAN/OneDrive/Desktop/New%20folder/market-service.js)
- Add calculation algorithms for:
  - **VWAP** (Volume Weighted Average Price)
  - **ADX(14)** (Average Directional Index with +DI and -DI)
  - **Pivot Points** (Standard Pivot, S1, S2, S3, R1, R2, R3, and Camarilla H3/H4/L3/L4)
  - **Stochastic Oscillator** (%K and %D)
  - **Ichimoku Kinko Hyo** (Tenkan-Sen conversion line, Kijun-Sen baseline)
  - **ATR(14)** as an accessible numeric indicator
- Store historical series arrays on the stock object (`stock.series = { close: [...], rsi: [...], ... }`) so offset lookups `[-1]`, `[-2]`, `[-5]` can evaluate historical indicators precisely.

#### [MODIFY] [scans.js](file:///c:/Users/TEJAS%20KUMAR%20DEWANGAN/OneDrive/Desktop/New%20folder/scans.js)
- Update `evaluateCondition(stock, condition)` to support:
  - `condition.leftOffset` (e.g. `0`, `-1`, `-2`, `-3`)
  - `condition.rightOffset` (e.g. `0`, `-1`, `-2`, `-3`)
  - Resolving indicators from historical candle bars or indicator series when an offset is specified.
- Support **Nested Filter Groups**:
  - If `scanDef.filterGroups` exists:
    - Evaluate each group individually with its own `group.passType` (`all` or `any`).
    - Combine groups using `scanDef.groupJoin` (`or` / `and`).
  - Gracefully fallback to flat `scanDef.filters` if no groups are defined.

